== (iii) the screening lattice = Z.(3,2) ==
  if screening contained [(3, 2), (0, 2)]: surviving functionals = NONE
  if screening contained [(3, 2), (3, 0)]: surviving functionals = NONE
  -> rank-2 screening kills ALL continuous charge,
     contradicting P8's screen-U(1): rank <= 1  (L3).
  (3,2) is primitive (gcd = 1): a rank-1 lattice
  containing it is exactly Z.(3,2).
  completeness: (tau, sigma, Y6) separates (a,b) mod (3,2)Z
  exactly: mismatches over [-6,6]^4 = 0
  -> THEOREM (E), conditional form: given L1 (collapse), L2
     (the QQQL receipt), L3 (P8 rank bound): the screening
     lattice is Z.(3,2); recordable charge data = (a,b) mod
     (3,2)Z with complete invariants (tau, sigma, Y6 = 3b-2a)
     - the S(U(3) x U(2)) structure, hence (Y-det), hence the
     Z6 lattice.  The only unproved piece is L1 at record
     scope: (E-coll), strictly smaller than the old (E-cond).

== (iv) the alternative rank-1 world (honest exhibit) ==
  a ledger certifying a (0,2)-seal instead (e^c nu^c-type)
  would screen Z.(0,2): surviving functionals = Z.(-1, 0):
  hypercharge would be Y = a (pure color-determinant).
  That world is mathematically consistent at this level; it
  is excluded by the LEDGER RECEIPTS - nature's sealed set
  contains baryon-lepton seals (B-L = 0 rows, P25) and no
  charged-lepton-pair seal - and by nothing else offered
  here.  The selection between the two rank-1 worlds is an
  empirical/dynamical fact (a candidate (M)-dynamics target),
  stated as such; what the conditional theorem removes is the
  TARGET-CALIBRATION: no congruence is copied from the SM
  anywhere in the chain.
